## THE RULINGS (the product owner, 2026-11-11 14:34, "29 quick recommendations accepted"; each ticket's own newest comment, read whole by the drafter; build from these words)
- **MPSCALC-202** (comment 41060): "Yes. Today a deploy can start an app that then refuses to boot." The pre-deploy overlay check (PRE-1) "is to refuse every price-overlay form the app itself refuses at start-up, and a malformed shape is to stop the check with one plain line. It must land before the first hosted price overlay exists." Ticket recommendation and acceptance (description): counts only, never a value; wrap so any shape error prints one PRE-1 STOP line and exits 1; say "PRE-1 stopped the deploy" for any non-zero result; "one shared rule both readers are tested against" is the better shape. Comment 39564 and 39647 (RELAYED): PRE-1 passes itemClass given as a number and an absent itemClass, which the app refuses.
- **MPSCALC-222, 103, 226** (comments 41058, 41057, 41059, the same ruling): "Both. An older package hides submitted quotes and drops new rows; the refusal makes the rule enforceable." **Roll forward only is the standing rule** for the hosted calculator, and the deploy is to refuse an older package once new-type rows (care packs, staging) exist. 222 adds (comment 39648, RELAYED): the refusal needs a COUNT of Care pack and Staging rows (quotes, snapshots, overlay), "a deploy-package.py subcommand beside PRE-1, so the rollback rule reads a command, not a seat's one-off script". Each note says: "Not built: the deploy refusal is queued as its own change with its own review; nothing is put on a host by this note."
- **Not in this kit** (THE CUT below): MPSCALC-224 (ruled: ship the patched Xml assembly in the package), MPSCALC-223 (no ruling comment; runbook text), MPSCALC-349 (no comment at all; a comment-line confirmation on SDK 10.0.404).

